  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The number of ways in which <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>21</mn></math> identical apples can be distributed among three children such that each child gets at least <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> apples, is</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>406</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>130</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>142</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>136</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let us initially distribute <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> apples to each children.</p><p>So, the remaining <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn></math> apples are to be distributed such that each children can get any number of apples.</p><p>So, the required number of ways will be given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mmultiscripts></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mrow><mn>15</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mmultiscripts></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>17</mn></mmultiscripts></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>17</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>136</mn></math></p>"
  }
